From: =?UTF-8?q?John=20T=C3=B6rnblom?= <john.tornblom@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:35:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/13] radv, vulkan/util: RADV is the PS4's libvulkan.so.1

The console has no Vulkan loader. There, RADV is built as libvulkan.so.1,
which exports the Vulkan API itself: vk_exports_gen.py generates the
functions the Khronos loader exports (core 1.0-1.4, VK_KHR_surface,
VK_KHR_swapchain, VK_KHR_display, VK_KHR_display_swapchain), each
forwarding through the dispatch table of the runtime object behind its
handle, so it reaches what vkGet*ProcAddr return. Only vk* and vk_icd*
are exported (vulkan.sym).

Programs link it with pkg-config vulkan, or dlopen("libvulkan.so.1") as
SDL and others do on Linux; the soname is the loader's, and so is the
version of the library and of vulkan.pc, the headers'
(1.4.<VK_HEADER_VERSION>). vulkan.pc also names the system modules RADV
calls (-lSceGnmDriver -lSceVideoOut), and the library links their stubs,
so the SDK's crt initializes them through libSceSysmodule.

The console build requires -Dradv-build-id: RADV names its shader cache
after its binary's build id, found through dl_iterate_phdr, which the
console does not have; without it there was silently no device.

A Linux host build of the PS4 winsys stays an ICD for the Khronos loader.

